ah, `float`. a cursed property from the dawn of time, when we built layouts with table cells and prayer. you've basically stumbled into a digital archaeological site.

the reason it breaks everything is that `float` was never meant for layout. it was designed to do one thing: make text wrap around an image, like in a newspaper. when you apply `float: left` or `float: right` to an element, you're yanking it out of the normal document flow.

